#X msg 700 5860 === STEP-13-of-26 === Modal safety timeout;
#X msg 700 5910 PASS IF: The surface turns green and then clears itself about thirty seconds later with nothing sent to it. Do not press GO -- sit and watch it.;
#X msg 700 5960 >>> press GO to run step 13 of 26;
#X obj 240 6030 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 6120 select 14;
#X obj 240 6120 t b b b;
#X msg 700 6120 === STEP-14-of-26 === Start the transport;
#X msg 700 6170 PASS IF: The white pad walks along the bottom row twice a second and the aux LED goes green. On the Mac the aux LED is not A button -- it is the numeric readout labelled aux-LED on the bottom row of the dev panel -- with a symbol box beside it spelling the colour. On the Mac tick enable-DSP first or the pad will not move. A BEATS line prints about ten seconds from now.;
#X msg 700 6220 >>> press GO to run step 14 of 26 -- then WAIT for the printed count before pressing GO again;
#X obj 240 6290 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 6380 select 15;
#X obj 240 6380 t b b b;
#X msg 700 6380 === STEP-15-of-26 === Beat row wrapping;
#X msg 700 6430 PASS IF: The white pad reaches the eighth pad and the next beat is back to the first -- with no gap and no stray light anywhere else. Nothing is sent for this step. Just watch one wrap go by.;
#X msg 700 6480 >>> press GO to run step 15 of 26;
#X obj 240 6550 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 6640 select 16;
#X obj 240 6640 t b b b;
#X msg 700 6640 === STEP-16-of-26 === Beat row at 240 BPM;
#X msg 700 6690 PASS IF: The white pad moves twice as fast. The BEATS line just printed should read about 20 beats and the next one about 40 beats. Expect A visible swing here and do not fail the step for it -- the row can only move on a 100 ms boundary so at 240 BPM it swings either way by 50 ms.;
#X msg 700 6740 >>> press GO to run step 16 of 26 -- then WAIT for the printed count before pressing GO again;
#X obj 240 6810 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 6900 select 17;
#X obj 240 6900 t b b b;
#X msg 700 6900 === STEP-17-of-26 === Back to 120 and stopped;
#X msg 700 6950 PASS IF: The second BEATS line reads about 40 and then the beat row slows to two a second. The pad must keep walking after the stop.;
#X msg 700 7000 >>> press GO to run step 17 of 26;
#X obj 240 7070 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 7160 select 18;
#X obj 240 7160 t b b b;
#X msg 700 7160 === STEP-18-of-26 === Pads and releases;
#X msg 700 7210 PASS IF: Every pad you press reports pad-NN on the OLED with its velocity. Releasing it reports the same name with a velocity of 0 instead. Numbering runs from 11 at the bottom left to 88 at the top right. Pressure on a held pad reports nothing and that is correct.;
#X msg 700 7260 >>> press GO to run step 18 of 26;
#X obj 240 7330 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 7420 select 19;
#X obj 240 7420 t b b b;
#X msg 700 7420 === STEP-19-of-26 === Ring buttons;
#X msg 700 7470 PASS IF: The ring buttons report lp-cc-NN. Check the top left corner reads 90 and the bottom row runs from 101 to 108 in order. CC 1 to 8 must be lit like everything else and must go blue under a modal and red under an alert. One button stays dark -- index 0 -- SETUP. It takes no colour and transmits nothing.;
#X msg 700 7520 >>> press GO to run step 19 of 26;
